# Continuous execution

The task is not complete when analysis, planning, documentation, project memory,
or a blocker list has been produced.

After establishing context and memory, immediately implement the highest-priority
verified requirement.

Do not stop after a phase summary, vertical slice, scaffold, or plan.

For each completed work item:

1. inspect the canonical implementation,
2. implement the full safe change,
3. add or update migrations,
4. add regression tests,
5. run relevant verification,
6. update project memory,
7. continue to the next highest-priority item.

Do not ask for permission between work items.

Only external credentials, unavailable third-party production environments, or
a genuine destructive ambiguity may remain as documented external verification.

A task is not complete because code was written. It is complete only when the
implementation, database, authorization, tests, documentation, and memory agree.
